{"chunk_id": "25eccde386e8", "text": "Satyaki reveals to Krishna, Dhritarashtra, and Vidura that Duryodhana and his allies secretly plan to seize Krishna by force in the Kuru court. The scheme is mocked as foolish\u2014like trying to grasp fire with cloth. Vidura warns Dhritarashtra that such an attempt will doom his sons, since Krishna is invincible and yet too righteous to retaliate with unjust violence. Krishna calmly confirms this: though he has the power to subdue them all and hand them to the Pandavas, he refuses to commit a wrongful act in the king\u2019s presence. Alarmed, Dhritarashtra summons Duryodhana and rebukes him, comparing the attempt to seizing the wind or reaching the moon. Vidura reinforces the warning by recounting Krishna\u2019s divine feats and victories over demons and kings, emphasizing that attacking him would bring certain destruction.\nSatyaki exposes a plot to seize Krishna; Vidura and Dhritarashtra warn Duryodhana of Krishna\u2019s invincible power, but Krishna calmly permits them to try.\nThemes: arrogance of Duryodhana, divine power of Krishna, warnings ignored, dharma vs ambition", "vector": [0.0022296777460724115, -0.019451668485999107, -0.0072439308278262615, 0.0005498526734299958, -0.014097752049565315, 0.03083210624754429, -0.022195888683199883, -0.02816860005259514, -0.01220101211220026, -0.005912177264690399, 0.023729421198368073, -0.005606143269687891, 0.0204740259796381, 0.015698546543717384, -0.015577477402985096, 0.001144265290349722, 0.05109089985489845, -0.025195695459842682, 0.029137147590517998, -0.031612325459718704, 0.0007554168696515262, -0.00035626921453513205, -0.010055409744381905, 0.016828518360853195, -0.009759464301168919, 0.02523605152964592, 0.006228300742805004, -0.0329575315117836, 0.012449875473976135, -0.021698161959648132, -0.009826725348830223, 0.0084882453083992, 0.017770161852240562, -0.00719012226909399, -0.03056306578218937, -0.006618410348892212, 0.0044761705212295055, -0.016532573848962784, -0.000